---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TechniqueDirectory from '../../../components/patterns/TechniqueDirectory.astro';
import TechniqueExperiment from '../../../components/patterns/TechniqueExperiment.astro';
import {techniques,prototypeRoot} from '../../../data/pattern-techniques';
import {resolveTechniques} from '../../../lib/pattern-techniques';
import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';
import '../../../styles/pattern-library.css';
import '../../../styles/pattern-prototype.css';
export function getStaticPaths(){
 if(import.meta.env.PROD&&process.env.PATTERN_PROTOTYPE!=='1')return [];
 return [{params:{technique:undefined},props:{slug:null}},...techniques.map(t=>({params:{technique:t.slug},props:{slug:t.slug}}))];
}
const {slug}=Astro.props;
const resolved=resolveTechniques(await getCollection('patterns'));
const technique=slug?resolved.find(t=>t.slug===slug):undefined;
if(slug&&!technique)throw Error('Unknown prototype technique');
const machineNames:Record<string,string>={'sinclair-zx-spectrum':'ZX Spectrum','commodore-64':'Commodore 64','commodore-amiga':'Amiga','nintendo-nes':'NES','cross-platform':'Shared technique'};
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Pattern Library',href:'/patterns/'},{label:'Prototype',...(technique?{href:prototypeRoot}:{})},...(technique?[{label:technique.title}]:[])];
---
<Layout title={`${technique?.title??'Connected techniques'} | Pattern Library prototype`} description={technique?.summary??'Four techniques, from reading a control to choosing a pursuer’s next turn.'} masthead={false} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} noindex>
 <div class="pattern-library technique-prototype" data-pagefind-ignore="all">
 {!technique?<>
  <header class="pattern-opening"><h1>Make one part<br/>work.</h1><div><p>Read a control. Catch a new press. Give it a sound.</p><p>Start with the job you need, then choose the code for your machine. Follow a connection when the next job becomes useful.</p><p class="prototype-note">Prototype for review · four techniques. The <a href="/patterns/">current Pattern Library</a> keeps its existing pages and addresses.</p></div></header>
  <section class="technique-chain" aria-labelledby="chain-title"><div><h2 id="chain-title">Three jobs, one response.</h2><p>A machine reader tells us what is held. A comparison finds the new press. A sound driver makes the response.</p></div><ol>{resolved.slice(0,3).map((t,i)=><li><span>{['Sample the controls','Find the new press','Trigger the response'][i]}</span><a href={`${prototypeRoot}${t.slug}/`}>{t.title}</a></li>)}</ol></section>
  <TechniqueDirectory/>
  <TechniqueExperiment kind="input"/>
  <footer class="pattern-next"><h2>Connections, without a compulsory course.</h2><p>You can use a joystick reader on its own. You can follow it to press detection. The <a href={`${prototypeRoot}choose-a-target/`}>pursuit experiment</a> makes another separation visible: where to aim, and how to choose a turn.</p><p><a href="/patterns/">Browse all existing patterns</a> · <a href="/vault/studies/pac-man/">Read the Pac-Man study</a></p></footer>
 </>:<>
  <header class="pattern-reading-header"><h1>{technique.title}</h1><p class="pattern-summary">{technique.task}</p><p>{technique.summary}</p><p class="prototype-note">Technique page prototype · <a href={prototypeRoot}>Back to the four techniques</a></p></header>
  <div class="technique-explanation"><p>{technique.explanation}</p><h2>What the pieces agree on</h2><p>{technique.contract}</p></div>
  <TechniqueExperiment kind={technique.experiment}/>
  <section class="implementation-section" aria-labelledby="implementations-title"><h2 id="implementations-title">{technique.implementations.length?'Choose an implementation':'The implementation in this prototype'}</h2>
   {technique.implementations.length?<><p>These are existing entries. Their code and evidence stay with them; the technique page connects the jobs without copying the listings.</p><ul class="implementation-list">{technique.implementations.map(i=><li><div><h3><a href={`/patterns/${i.id}/`}>{i.entry.data.title}</a></h3><p>{machineNames[i.entry.data.platform]} · {i.language}</p></div><div><strong>{i.evidence==='emulator-executed'?'Assembled and emulator-executed':'Illustrative listing'}</strong><p>{i.note}</p><p><a href={`/patterns/${i.id}/`}>Read the code, contract and evidence</a></p></div></li>)}</ul></>:<><p>This original JavaScript experiment runs in the browser. It has no claimed C64, Spectrum, Amiga or NES implementation. The board shows each candidate’s squared distance and the stated tie-break.</p><p><a href="/vault/studies/pac-man/">The Pac-Man study</a> explores the historical rules, their quirks and the game around them. This experiment deliberately simplifies them.</p></>}
  </section>
  <section class="technique-explanation"><h2>Fit it into a game</h2><p>{technique.slug==='read-input'?'Read once at an agreed point in the update. Store the sample so movement and press detection see the same controls. Write an explicit adapter if the reader returns a different format.':technique.slug==='detect-presses'?'Use the stored current sample for continuous actions and the new-press result for single actions. Do not advance the history separately in each consumer.':technique.slug==='trigger-sound'?'Let the game emit an event, then hand it to the chosen driver. Read its stopping and ownership contract before connecting it to a running game.':'Keep target selection separate from legal movement. A new target rule can reuse the same turn chooser, but obstacles may demand a route-finding algorithm instead.'}</p>
   {technique.next.length>0&&<><h3>A useful next job</h3><ul>{technique.next.map(slug=>{const next=techniques.find(t=>t.slug===slug)!;return <li><a href={`${prototypeRoot}${slug}/`}>{next.title}</a> — {next.task}</li>;})}</ul></>}
   {technique.slug==='trigger-sound'&&<p>For a wider comparison, see <a href="/patterns/cross-platform/audio/making-a-sound/">Four Ways to Make a Sound</a> and the <a href="/patterns/cross-platform/audio/tune-sequencer/">tune sequencer</a>. These are onward reading, not additional completed prototype implementations.</p>}
  </section>
  <footer class="pattern-next"><p><a href={prototypeRoot}>All four techniques</a> · <a href="/patterns/">Current Pattern Library</a></p></footer>
 </>}
 </div>
</Layout>
